<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jaan Poska</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1866">1866</a>–<a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jaan Poska was an Estonian lawyer and statesman, mayor of Reval (Tallinn), who became commissar of the Autonomous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">Governorate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a> created in 1917 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/february-revolution">February Revolution</a>. He later served in the provisional government of the Republic of Estonia, and as head of the Estonian delegation he signed the Treaty of Tartu with Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1920, which recognised Estonian independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jaan-poska.jpg" alt="Jaan Poska" width="320" height="517" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Virumaa_Muuseumid_RM_F_1358_1,_Jaan_Poska.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
